#3. Consumer finance ecology: the right but painful retreat

** 2025 Contribution for year: ~43.2 billion (estimated) ~12.1% Trend: active contraction**

Credit guarantee insurance (i.e. "The borrower does not pay, the insurance company pays) was once one of the most profitable products for the public. The risk profile of this business is completely different from property insurance – it is essentially a disguised consumer finance** and there is a huge risk for asset quality.

The huge loss of the public security sector in 2022 was 13.56 billion yuan, largely due to the sharp rise in the payment of credit guarantee insurance. Management now expects that the premium for this block will fall in 2026 in comparison to the previous year **50-60%**.

** This is the right strategic choice.** A financial firm that does the risk of consumer finance is in itself doing a bad job. Proactive contractions, while reducing premium increases, improve overall aggregate cost rates.

